remstart
    THE FAST
    another hidden thing. nothing in the game says that it is there. the routines are in
    fish_routines_fast, and the tests are in fish_tests_fast.

    the upgrade screen has a line that takes none of the cards. taking nothing is a fast, and the
    game counts how many upgrade screens in a row have been left that way: FAST_STREAK. taking a card
    ends the fast, and so does dropping a passive. dealing the cards again does not.
    the line says how long the fast has been: it has a dot after it for every time.

    THE LADDER. a fast that is long enough changes what the next upgrade screen offers. these are
    the rungs, by how long the fast is when the screen comes up. FAST_RUNG is the one that is up.
        2   "rotate", and nothing else
        4   "rotate", or "open book"
        6   "oceanic oath", and nothing else
    a rung only offers what the player does not have. the first one offers "open book" to a player
    who has "rotate" already, and a rung that has nothing left to offer is an upgrade screen like any
    other. the cards of a rung can not be dealt again.
    the screens in between are the usual ones. leaving the oath is the end of the fast: it starts
    over from nothing. the praise of the coral is sung when a rung comes up. see fastOpen.
    the three cards are never dealt any other way. FAST_CARD_FROM is the first of them, and
    assign_ability_selection, in fish_routines_ability, passes over every card from there on.

    ROTATE. a special move. the button is held, and the cursor is walked: one way, for as far as the
    player likes, and then a turn to one side, for as far as the player likes. the cell that it
    started on and the cell that it is on are two corners of a box. when the button is let go, the
    fish around the edge of the box all go one cell along it, the way that the cursor turned: right
    and then down is clockwise. a second turn does the same as letting go. going back along a leg
    takes it back, and a walk that is back where it started is no move at all.
    a walk that never turned has no box. nothing happens, and the move is not used up.
    it never has to recharge. it counts as one move, and it is not a swap: the multiplier and the tide leave it alone, and the
    steps of the walk are not the steps of a song. an outline shows the box while it is being walked.
    rotateWants and rotateTook follow the walk, for process_input, in fish_routines_input. doRotate
    turns the box.

    OPEN BOOK. an instant. from then on, the upgrade screen does not deal cards. it lays out every
    card that could have been dealt, in a grid like the one of the codec, and the player takes any
    one of them. see THE BOOK, further down.

    OCEANIC OATH. a passive. "Take only memories. No more upgrades at round breaks. Multiplier will
    never go down." no upgrade screen comes up again: a round that is won goes straight on to the
    next, the way that it does in a zen game. and a swap that pops nothing still empties the bar of
    the multiplier, but it never takes one off of the multiplier itself. fastOath says if it is taken.

    THE MODIFIERS. things that a game can have had happen in it, which are not how it ended. a game
    has any number of them. GAME_MODS is the ones that the game that is being played has had, added
    up: each one is a power of two. they are saved with the game, they go onto the table of high
    scores with it, and to Steam. see THE MODIFIERS ON THE TABLES, further down.
        MOD_OATH    the "oceanic oath" was taken
        MOD_CORAL   coral grew, of either kind
        MOD_NIGHT   night fell
        MOD_BEAT    a move was made in time with a tune. see THE DANCE in fish_headers.
    modSet, in fish_routines_fast, is how a game gets one.
remend

` the cards. they go after the cards that there were before, which keep their numbers.
#constant FAST_CARD_FROM 32
global ABILITY_INDEX_MOVE_ROTATE = 32
#constant ABILITY_INDEX_OPEN_BOOK 33
global ABILITY_INDEX_OATH = 34

` THE LADDER
global FAST_STREAK = 0 `how many upgrade screens in a row have been left with nothing. it is saved with the game.
global FAST_RUNG = 0 `the rung that the upgrade screen that is up is, or 0 for an upgrade screen like any other
global FAST_RUNG_ROTATE = 2 `how long the fast is when each rung comes up
global FAST_RUNG_BOOK = 4
global FAST_RUNG_OATH = 6
global dim FAST_OFFER(4) `the cards of the rung that is up
global FAST_OFFER_COUNT = 0
global SAVE_PREF_FAST = 50 `where the fast of the saved game is kept, after SAVE_PREF: how long it is, and then the modifiers

` ROTATE
global ROTATE_COOLDOWN = 0 `how many moves it takes to recharge. it never has to.
global ROTATE_TIME = 220 `how long the fish take to go around, in milliseconds
global ROTATE_ON = 0 `1 while the box is being walked
global ROTATE_SLOT = -1 `the slot of the move that is walking it
global ROTATE_FROM_X = 0 `the cell that the walk started on
global ROTATE_FROM_Y = 0
global ROTATE_AXIS = 0 `which way the first leg went: 1 for across, and 2 for up or down
global ROTATE_BOX as infoBorder `the outline of the box
global ROTATE_BOX_MADE = 0 `1 once the outline has been made. it is made the first time that it is needed.
global ROTATE_LAST_COUNT = 0 `how many fish the last one moved. 0 means that there was no box. the tests read this.
global ROTATE_LAST_CLOCKWISE = 0 `and which way they went
global dim ROTATE_RING(80) `the cells around the edge of the box, in the order that the fish go along it
global ROTATE_RING_COUNT = 0
global ROTATE_TWEEN_ID = 0

` THE MODIFIERS
#constant MOD_OATH 1
#constant MOD_CORAL 2
#constant MOD_NIGHT 4
#constant MOD_BEAT 8
#constant MOD_COUNT 4
#constant MOD_ALL 15
global GAME_MODS = 0 `the modifiers of the game that is being played, added up

remstart
    THE BOOK. the page that the upgrade screen has for a player with the "open book" card: every card
    that could have been dealt, as a grid of little pictures, like the grid of the codec, with the
    name of the highlighted one under the grid, and what it does. the player takes any one of them.
    it is what the upgrade screen comes up as. the pause key goes back to the cards that were dealt,
    and the lines under them: taking nothing is still there, and so is dropping a passive. the line
    that deals new cards opens the book again in place of that, since there is nothing to deal for.
    a rung of the fast is not the book. it has its own cards.
    the routines are in fish_routines_book. like the page that drops a passive, it borrows the title
    and the bright outline of the upgrade screen, and is drawn to the same render target.
    cardCanBeDealt, in fish_routines_fast, says which cards are in it. it has the same rules that
    assign_ability_selection, in fish_routines_ability, deals by, and the two have to be kept the same by hand.
remend
global BOOK_ROOM = 32 `how many cards there is room for, which is every card that can be dealt
global BOOK_COLUMNS = 8 `how many there are on a row of the grid
global BOOK_TILE = 30 `how far apart the tiles of the grid are
global BOOK_TOP = 102 `where the middle of the first row is
global BOOK_COUNT = 0 `how many cards are in it
global dim BOOK_CARDS(32) `and which they are
global dim BOOK_SPRITES(32) `the picture of every one
global BOOK_SELECTED = 0 `the one that is highlighted
global BOOK_PICK = -1 `the card that was taken from it, or -1 when the player went back
global BOOK_INSTANT = 0 `1 to put the page up without the cards shrinking away first, for when the upgrade screen comes up as the book
global BOOK_FADE_TWEEN_ID = 0 `0 when the page is put away, and 1 when it is showing
global BOOK_NAME_TEXT_ID = 0
global BOOK_KIND_TEXT_ID = 0
global BOOK_DESC_TEXT_ID = 0
global BOOK_PANEL_SPRITE = 0 `the dark panel that the grid and the words are on

remstart
    THE MODIFIERS ON THE TABLES. the modifiers of a game go onto the table of high scores with it,
    in the same number as its initials and the badge of its ending: they are how many times
    HISCORE_MOD_STEP is added on top of those. see HISCORE_BADGE_STEP in fish_headers. getScoreMods,
    in fish_routines_fast, takes them out again. on Steam they are four of the flags of the score,
    from STEAM_FLAG_MODS on, which an older version of the game does not look at.
    every row of a table has a little picture for each modifier that its game had, in a strip of
    their own to the right of the table, one column for each modifier. modsDrawTable draws them.
    the upgrades of the fast are not written in the log of a game, so the log of somebody else's
    game does not give the cards away. logUpgrade, in fish_routines_highscores, passes over them.

    A MODIFIER THAT THE PLAYER HAS NOT HAD is not given away, the same as an ending that the player
    has not got to: its picture on a row is a question mark, and it has no tile. the ones that the
    player has had, in any game, are kept in the preferences, added up, at PREF_MODS_KNOWN.

    THE TILES OF THE MODIFIERS. every modifier that the player has had has a tile, after the tiles of
    the endings. see THE ENDINGS THAT ARE SHOWN in fish_headers. a tile that is switched off leaves
    the games that had that modifier out of the table. HISCORE_TILE_ENDING is HISCORE_MOD_TILE plus
    the number of the modifier for those tiles, counting from 0, and HISCORE_ENDING_SHOWN has
    whether they are switched on at the same place. isModsShown says if a game is shown.
remend
global HISCORE_MOD_STEP = 80000 `more than the initials and any badge of an ending come to
global HISCORE_MOD_TILE = 10 `the first of the numbers that the tiles of the modifiers have
global STEAM_FLAG_MODS = 8 `the first of the four flags that are the modifiers
#constant PREF_MODS_KNOWN 15
global MODS_KNOWN = 0 `the modifiers that the player has had in any game, added up. modsLoadKnown reads it.
global dim MOD_TEX(4) `the picture of every modifier. Tools/fast_art_gen.py draws them.
global dim MOD_COLOR(4) `and its color
global HISCORE_MOD_MADE = 0 `1 once the pictures of the rows have been made. they are made the first time that a table is shown.
global dim HISCORE_MOD_SPRITES(32) `for every row of the table, a picture for every modifier
global HISCORE_MOD_BACK_SPRITE = 0 `the strip that they are on
global HISCORE_MOD_SIZE = 12 `how big one of the pictures is, and how far apart they are
